L10 — LLVM pr23135 source definedness, 2026-10-13
=================================================

Scope: the evidence for one source-bound disposition. The unchanged LLVM
original executes signed int overflow in a GNU vector lane. The disposition
is not-applicable (source undefined behavior). It is not a PASS. It follows
the owner's decision of 2026-10-13
(docs/archive/notebook/rules-20261013/DECISIONS.md, row L10) and the packet
docs/archive/notebook/rules-20261013/l10-pr23135-definedness.md. Points 1 to
6 below are the six-point B01 source-UB threshold. No compiler, source,
command, expected output, receipt or historical count changes.

