  differ in one line:
    < /* { dg-options "-Wno-psabi" } */
    > /* { dg-options "-Wno-psabi -fwrapv" } */
  The LLVM lit harness does not read dg-options.

Labeled control: -fwrapv. This is NOT the original's PASS.
  The recorded command does not request -fwrapv. These runs only show that
  EvoCC computes the expected values when wrap-around is requested.
  Both interpreters, each F with -fwrapv: print 0, exit 0.
  Linux native, each F with -fwrapv: exit 0. Assembly SHA256: -O0
    e9f022bbc3bb34b228b629046bbdad1e880b40dfcf6ad63ca169d9c468a204cd;
    -O2 and the lane's options (identical)
    8060766193849c8fb429321bd2095e097c420c902c27d326ef2cecc2396ee887.
    Neither has an smull instruction.
  Darwin native, each F with -fwrapv: exit 0.

Plain reference runs (no sanitizer)
  gcc-14 and clang-19, -std=gnu11 -O0|-O2 -w -Wno-psabi and ORIG, each with
  and without -fwrapv: 12 compilations exit 0 and 12 runs exit 0. Apple
  clang at -O0 and -O2, with and without -fwrapv: 4 runs exit 0. An exit 0
  without -fwrapv shows what that compiler did. It is not evidence of
  definedness.

